{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788197815086,"sessionID":"ses_fa71b57adffe2ekWe4aNvJvuc4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_2104e253147146ef87b318cb","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"python3 --version && python3 -c \"import flask\" 2>&1; python3 -c \"import fastapi\" 2>&1; python3 -c \"import pytest\" 2>&1"},"output":"Python 3.12.12\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<string>\", line 1, in <module>\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'flask'\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<string>\", line 1, in <module>\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'fastapi'\n","metadata":{"output":"Python 3.12.12\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<string>\", line 1, in <module>\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'flask'\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<string>\", line 1, in <module>\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'fastapi'\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"python3 --version && python3 -c \"import flask\" 2>&1; python3 -c \"import fastapi\" 2>&1; python3 -c \"import pytest\" 2>&1","time":{"start":1788197814952,"end":1788197815085}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The task is to create a REST API service for managing a book collection in Python. Requirements:\n\n1. POST /books — Create a new book (title, author, year, isbn)\n2. GET /books — List all books (support ?author= filter)\n3. GET /books/{id} — Get a single book by ID\n4. PUT /books/{id} — Update a book\n5. DELETE /books/{id} — Delete a book\n6. Store data in SQLite\n7. JSON responses with appropriate HTTP status codes\n8. Input validation (title and author required)\n9. Health check endpoint: GET /health\n10. README.md with setup and run instructions\n11. At least 3 unit/integration tests\n\nThe task says \"Use the specified language and framework\" — language is Python. Framework isn't specified beyond that, so I'll pick something sensible. FastAPI is a great choice, but it requires installing dependencies. Alternatively, I could use Flask. Or I could use Python's standard library only (http.server) which requires no dependencies at all — that would make \"the code builds and tests pass\" trivially verifiable.\n\nLet me check what's available in the environment first. Let me check Python version and whether Flask/FastAPI are installed.\n\nActually, using stdlib-only (http.server + sqlite3) would be robust — no dependency install needed, no version conflicts. But a \"REST API service\" is more idiomatically done with Flask/FastAPI. Let me check what's available.\n\nLet me check the environment first.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_058e54231001TLmPRKKOwYuATN","sessionID":"ses_fa71b57adffe2ekWe4aNvJvuc4","messageID":"msg_058e50d3a001jgxcTN881zvngy"}}
